WEBVTT

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.040
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.790
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.410
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:25.660
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:31.080
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.160
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:39.700
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.700
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.830
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:53.410
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:59.910
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:05.750
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:11.660
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:16.750
<i>Lord of crime hora yume no ikenie</i>
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:29.000
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.700
"The 'Noahtic' Act 1"

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.250
Hey, wait up!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.080
Tch!

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.700
Why is there so much refuse here?

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.870
This is the maiden voyage
of a luxury cruise liner.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.160
They are all passengers, sir.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.830
There are three different classes
of passenger cabins,

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.580
and a number of the rooms available
are moderately priced.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.660
I'm saying that this is a ship that no one
but noblemen should be able to board.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.370
Can't you tell simply by looking
at her grand form?

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:33.330
The <i>Noahtic</i>--a ship truly worthy
to take on the name of Noah.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.500
Do <i>you </i>think that the Noah that appears
in the Bible, the one who was on the Ark,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.160
was a commoner?

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.120
Uh...

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.950
Noah was chosen of God!

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.370
Which is to say, a nobleman, like me!

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.290
Just look.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.870
Many noblemen are thronging to board this ship.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.450
So if, by some chance, a great flood
were to hit London whilst we're at sea,

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:01.330
our country would not face too much difficulty.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.330
Don't you agree?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.580
The only ones left behind
would be the dregs of society.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:12.040
If they were swallowed up in the waves and
swept away, things would be much more agreeable.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.040
Oh, it's Lord Enders!

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:19.040
Imagine, running into Lord Enders here!

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.000
It is an honour to meet you!

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.500
Well, well, fancy having lovely ladies
like you coming along.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.660
We are here to watch the ballet
being performed aboard this ship!

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.040
It will be the world's first seagoing ballet!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.660
This is something we simply cannot pass up!

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.620
You are quite the curious young ladies.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:40.290
Very well, let's see about
getting aboard this ark--

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:45.040
built especially for those
of us carrying noble blood.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.910
I can't wait!

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:50.750
Target is commencing boarding
at the scheduled time.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.410
Well, let's get this show started.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:09.700
I've been thinking about how imbalanced
this country is for a long time.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:13.040
It is unnecessary to reiterate that
the principal cause of this imbalance

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.700
is the class system that is enjoyed
by a handful of aristocrats.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.500
We must contend against it.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.830
That's all well and true, but who
do we fight, and how do we do it?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.580
The system is not immediately alterable.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.000
However, there <i>is </i>something
that we can begin to do right away.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:38.830
We can plunge London down into the depths
of Hell, and turn it into a crime-filled city.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.910
Oi, explain it so we can understand.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:49.870
How does that lead to our goal
of improving the country?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:55.000
Crime is not the end; it is the means, Moran.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.790
As I said earlier, we cannot change
the system in a trice.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:03.250
However, we can change
the minds of men in an instant.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.950
Minds?

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:10.000
People have a wide range of emotions,
and are also creatures who act upon them.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.830
Further, the thing that spurs the human
mind to action above all else...

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.700
...is... death.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:23.580
I agree, Will. Death is more
instrumental than anything.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:29.950
William, if my death is required for
your plan, I offer it to you at any time.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.790
The same goes for you, right?

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.830
The citizens of London are about to witness

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:39.290
the many crimes and deaths
that I have tailored for them.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.910
Which is to say...

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:53.250
...the city shall be turned into
a stage through crime,

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:56.750
and its citizens shall be an audience
bearing witness to those crimes.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.000
The city of London itself will become a theatre?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.870
And the subject matter we
shall present our audience

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:08.450
will be deaths that most vividly expose
the imbalance of the world.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:13.790
It is the deaths that we choreograph,
dramatise, and give significance to

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:18.500
that will truly open the eyes
of this country's people.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.540
We're the ones who will be
pulling the trigger, then?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.700
This should be interesting.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.040
Now, the time has come for the curtain to rise.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:34.200
If this forthcoming production
on the big stage is a success,

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.910
it will mark a large step toward
the world for which we are striving.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:43.700
Now, allow me to present you
with our first illustrious star...

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.120
...Count Blitz Enders.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.120
Stand aside.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.200
Hey! What are you trying to board first for?!

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.910
We were here first! Get to the end of the line!

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:10.620
Do you realise to whom you are speaking?

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:14.330
Know your place, you swine.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:15.750
What did you call me?!

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:21.000
I am most sorry for that, sir.
Please, go right on inside.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.120
For Heaven's sake, how aggravating.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:25.080
--You should just throw that whole
lot of upright-walking livestock

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.870
--What?! You're letting him on?!
Hey, you, get back here!
--You should just throw that whole
lot of upright-walking livestock

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:31.080
--What?! You're letting him on?!
Hey, you, get back here!
--into a hutch in the ship's larder, or something.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.910
The captain would like to extend
his welcome to all of you.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:46.290
This ship, the <i>Noahtic</i>, is now beginning
its pleasure cruise to Amsterdam.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:50.620
Moreover, tomorrow, the world's first
shipborne ballet will be performed.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:54.790
Please do enjoy the show
along with the rest of your voyage.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.950
How is our "event" coming along?

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:09.830
Heh. Brother, you're so impatient.
The curtain has just barely risen.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:14.040
I see. All right then, I think
I shall go and enjoy myself,

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.950
whilst looking forward to
the arrival of the climax.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:23.120
What?! You don't have a
dinner reservation for me?!

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.660
What is the meaning of this?!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.080
I am terribly sorry, sir. Apparently,
there has been a slight mix-up.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.660
A mix-up?!

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:35.120
S-Sir, I can show you to the restaurant
on the lower deck right away, if you like--

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:36.500
Don't be absurd!

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.000
Are you telling me I should go and fill my face
together with that livestock in the dining mess?

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.200
Oh, no, sir, not at all!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.000
I am of the privileged class,
and I will have no one stand in my way!

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.160
Is that clear?

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:52.500
Y-Yes, sir. Um, in that case,
please wait just a moment.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.080
I will see to finding you a seat at once.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.290
F-Forgive me, my lord!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:08.000
If you ever cross my path again,
I will kill you.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Wah! Mummy!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.000
There now, what's the matter?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:18.160
If there are commoners this close to
the first-class passenger restaurant,

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:22.000
it means that they're
crawling all over this ship.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:24.750
That was unfortunate.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.370
Feel free to use mine, if you like.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.290
Ah, thanks.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:34.290
I am Moriarty. William James Moriarty.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:38.660
Moriarty? I've heard that name before.
The army, as I recall.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.950
That would be my older brother, Albert.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.290
He is also on board;
I will have to introduce you later.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.160
Lord Enders...

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.080
We have a table ready for you. This way, please.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.580
Ah. I'll see you around.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:57.910
What kind of ship are you running here?
What possible excuse could you have for this?

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.000
That's the way you wanted it?

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:10.200
Yeah, well played. Please continue to
annoy the count as much as possible.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:13.660
That's our agreement,
and I have no problem with it,

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:15.950
but why do you want me acting like this?

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:19.080
Isn't this a lot of bother to go to
just to pester somebody?

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:25.700
"Don't ask why." That was part
of the contract, remember?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:31.000
Well, as long as I get paid,
I've got no quarrel with it.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.790
Thomas Michaelson...

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:41.700
...a habitual burglar, who has also committed...

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:46.120
...rape, and even murder
in the course of his crimes.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:52.950
We will take your depraved life...
and make good use of it.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:05.250
Why, Count Moriarty,
fancy running into you on this ship, as well.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:09.370
If it were only a luxury liner,
I would not have been so interested,

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.540
but I heard there was going to
be a magnificent attraction.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:16.000
You mean the world's first
shipborne ballet, right?

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:20.080
That was my reason for coming, as well.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:26.540
You don't say. As a ballet aficionado,
you could not pass this up?

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:32.290
Precisely right. I'll admit, even now,
I'm looking forward to seeing

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:34.830
what sort of show they're going to put on.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:38.080
Yes. I'm sure...

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:41.080
...it will end up being something spectacular.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:51.250
Blitz Enders, you have a telegram, sir.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:02.830
Some unwelcome news should be
reaching the target right about now.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:22.750
Amazing! How did you know
that gentleman was a soldier?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:25.750
Did you happen to know that beforehand?

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:27.620
Well then, what about that man?

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.120
Can you guess what line of work he is in?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.290
Yeah, I got it.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.040
You really do?

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.080
If you're right this time,
that will be ten in a row!

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:44.830
Excuse us, sir, we were just settling a bet.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:46.620
A bet, you say?

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:52.040
Yes, to see if he can look at others walking by
and guess what their occupations are.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:56.290
Go on, tell us, quickly!
What does that gentleman do?

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:59.580
Oh, can't you tell already?

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:02.040
His line of work...

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.250
...is as a mathematician.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:16.330
His line of work...

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.750
...is as a mathematician.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.830
What makes you think that?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.790
Please tell us your reasons!

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:28.120
Yeah, it's a hell of a spiral
staircase, isn't it?

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:30.450
I can see why you'd admire it.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:34.450
Right... Mr Mathematician?

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.620
What makes you think I am a mathematician?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.910
Huh? It's as clear as day.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:42.330
Whilst gazing at this
spiral staircase, your time,

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:45.830
your distance, and your angle told me so.

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:47.620
See here.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:52.290
This is a matter of simple deduction
based on observation and knowledge.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:56.290
Despite being absorbed in thought
as he was walking along,

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.370
he stopped when he got to the stairs.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:04.330
Almost as though he had found a sight
that caused the thought in his mind

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:07.160
to come to a momentary halt.

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:12.200
Indeed, the stairway is beautifully
adorned, and worth a look.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:16.080
But his attention was not focused
on the intricate ornamentation;

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:21.790
rather, he took a step back, and began
observing the staircase as a whole.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:24.620
What profession looks not on
the cosmetic beauty of the staircase

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:28.830
but is instead interested in its construction?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:34.500
An architect? Or perhaps a physicist?
No, on the contrary.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:38.040
His gaze did not fall upon the column.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.950
This was because his interest was not
with how the stairs were supported.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:46.750
So then, what was he looking at
that caused him to take a step back?

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:51.290
He wanted to see something.
He wanted to confirm something.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:56.790
Whether the curve traced by these stairs
was based on something or not.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:00.870
By which I mean... the golden ratio.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:07.080
Indeed. You are quite the keen observer.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:09.910
Your logical argument was a trifle forced,

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:13.500
but I do, in fact, teach
mathematics at university.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.870
Then you mean...

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:17.040
He was right again!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:21.790
Now then... permit me to try
the same with you now.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.950
Let's see, now...

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.750
It appears that you can play the violin.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:30.450
Nonetheless, you are not a musician.

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:34.700
Additionally, you are adept in fighting
and other physical abilities.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:38.200
Moreover, you have an interest
in scientific experiments...

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:44.040
...as well as a slight touch
of chemical dependency.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:50.500
You strike me as an Oxbridge man,

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:54.040
but your dialect is more in
the vein of the working class.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:58.750
No doubt because you
take pride in your ancestry.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:01.540
Your mother's side, in particular.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.120
Or am I mistaken?

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:06.250
How did you know?

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.910
Why...

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.450
...because it is obvious.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:19.620
You are a genuinely intriguing chap.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.450
I am?

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.370
Come on, let's go try on the upper deck now.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.950
Are we still doing this?

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:29.870
At this point, I want to see how many times
in a row you can guess correctly!

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:32.370
What's a fellow to do?

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:36.000
Well, see you around, mathematician.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.580
It's amazing, however often I see it!

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.870
--Hurry along, now!
--Is anything the matter?

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.330
No...

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:46.080
This should pose no great hindrance to our plan.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.040
How are you faring?

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.450
Our target is becoming considerably
agitated, right on schedule.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:54.120
Good. Keep it up.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:59.290
It will not be much longer before he
nears the end of his endurance.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:14.040
I wonder what is troubling Lord Enders.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:17.120
I understand he has had a rash of bad fortune.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.660
I heard he received a telegram
saying his cottage burnt down

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.700
and that there was some sort
of accident at his colliery.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.410
In any event, we had best
give him some space right now.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.500
Let's leave him to himself.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.080
Y-Yes.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:35.500
What is this? What is happening?

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.790
Everything has been exasperating
ever since I boarded this ship!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:42.950
It's as though there's a conspiracy
for nothing but calamity to befall me!

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.790
Damnation! I can't take any more!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.910
If only this were my hunting ground...!

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:55.790
No, why should I even think twice about it?

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.540
This is Noah's Ark.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:08.700
We, the nobility, are the only ones aboard
that could be called human.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:14.450
There are plenty of other animals aboard
that I could make my prey.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.330
You're sure about this, now?

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:31.200
I hurled some dreadful words at you
when we were boarding...

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.500
...and I would like to apologise.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.660
Heh. You aristocrats are so generous.

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:38.290
The liquor is in the inner stateroom.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:42.200
Whoo, first-class cabins sure are luxurious.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:51.290
This is incredible! Which one should
I start with? It's so hard to choose!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.620
This is too perfect!

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:57.330
I'll pretend to be soused afterward,
and once I'm ill-mannered with him again,

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:01.870
I'll be able to get the good
count even more nettled.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:05.700
All right, I'll start with this bottle, then.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:10.250
You're sure I can take this, then?

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:11.870
Yes.

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:13.540
Assuming...

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.950
...you survive, that is!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:22.160
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:26.700
You really are no different from an animal!

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.540
Even your cries before dying are ignoble!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.410
S-Stop...!

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:50.450
What a fine evening this has become.

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:55.410
There really is a different zest that goes
with killing with your own hands

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.410
as compared to hunting with a gun.

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:01.290
Perhaps I'll try that sometime
on my hunting ground.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:11.700
Sir... that special cut of meat
you ordered is ready.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:19.080
Also, the room has been left unlocked,
so whenever you feel inclined...

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.580
Thank you.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:31.660
Lord Enders?

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:36.040
It's Moriarty. Are you all right?

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:41.250
One of the ladies informed me that she
heard a shout coming from your room.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:44.200
I am here to make sure all is well.

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:45.950
Moriarty?!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:49.040
Th-This is bad! Not right now!

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:51.540
If he finds out I hunted him...!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:55.580
Oh, the door is open. I'm letting myself in.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.910
Wha--?! I know I locked that!

00:21:57.910 --> 00:21:59.410
Lord Enders, where are you?

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:01.700
J-Just a moment!

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:03.080
Oh, my...

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:13.790
This is...

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:15.910
...quite serious.

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:20.250
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:24.450
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:43.540
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:45.790
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:49.330
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:22:49.330 --> 00:22:52.540
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:56.040
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:59.660
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:03.410
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:08.250
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:11.910
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:13.580
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.370
<i>at the end</i>

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:18.540
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:22.790
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:29.410
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:30.910
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:37.750
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:43.370
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:45.750
<i>There is no turning back</i>

00:23:46.790 --> 00:23:52.450
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The 'Noahtic' Act 2."
